<title>NETHERLANDS: ING Polish asset manager wins permit.</title>
<headline>ING Polish asset manager wins permit.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank and financial services group ING said on Tuesday its ING BSK Asset Management subsidiary had won a permit from the Polish authorities to manage investment portfolios for third parties.</p>
<p>&quot;ING BSK Asset Management is the first specialised asset management company in Poland to be awarded a permit of this nature,&quot; ING said in a statement.</p>
<p>Asset management in Poland had previously been the preserve of Polish brokerages, it said.</p>
<p>ING BSK Asset Management is a 50-50 joint venture with Poland's Bank Slaski, in which ING holds a majority stake.</p>
